# 🤓: "Digital thread" (MBD/MBSE term) = continuous traceable data linkage across a
# system lifecycle. In b00t: every task, datum, guard hit, and A2A message is a node
# in the thread, queryable via the knowledge graph.
#
# OODA Loop mapping:
#   Observe  = OTEL metrics + guard-violations.jsonl + datum filter results
#   Orient   = knowledge graph query → datum type inference → tier routing
#   Decide   = OKR KR evaluation → next-task selection → resource gate
#   Act      = b00t task next → agent delegation → OTEL record → loop

## Problem

# b00t has all the primitives but they are not wired into a SELF-AWARE loop:
#
# 1. Context delta (PRD-002) → agents waste 20% on headers
# 2. Delegation macros (PRD-003) → @sm0l: still verbose
# 3. Self-improve loop (PRD-004) → not running
# 4. MBSE visualization (PRD-005) → datums are dark
# 5. CLIF/OWL2 (PRD-006) → first-order logic not queryable
# 6. ControlFlow ontology (PRD-008) → gates not typed
# 7. OTEL (PRD-009) → metrics not fed back
# 8. Postel hints (PRD-010) → normalizations not learned
#
# Each PRD is a shard of a unified system. The digital thread connects them:
# every capability is self-documented, measurable, and improvable by the hive itself.

## Finished State — OODA Handoff Loop

# The canonical b00t agentic loop is:
#
# ```
# b00t task next              ← Decide: what's the highest-priority unblocked task?
#   → sm0l: classify tier     ← Orient: is this sm0l/ch0nky/frontier?
#   → @tier: execute          ← Act: delegate with delegation macros (PRD-003)
#   → otel::record(CommandRun) ← Observe: metric captured
#   → okr eval                ← Observe: KR status updated
#   → b00t task done N        ← next iteration
# ```
#
# The `/next-task:N` handoff pattern encodes:
# - Current task completed
# - Artifacts verified (OTEL summary, test result)
# - Blockers identified
# - Next task ID pre-selected (lowest unblocked by priority)
# This becomes the agent "battle plan" that is both human-readable and machine-executable.

## PRD-002 Integration (Context Delta)

# llama-patch was abandoned because the source wasn't pre-formatted.
# tomllm fixed the format. The delta protocol is now the path:
#
# `b00t whoami --role=domain-architect` currently = 4K tokens (full AGENTS.md)
# With PRD-002 delta: base (cached) + 100-token role delta = 1.1K tokens
#
# PRD-002 is the SINGLE HIGHEST LEVERAGE item for reducing per-agent cost.
# Implement TomllmDelta::apply() in tomllm crate as first sub-task.
# Dogfood: this PRD datum itself should have a delta from ++abstract.prd.tomllm.

## A2A Service Fabric

# Agent-to-Agent (A2A) communication in b00t uses Redis IPC (existing b00t-ipc).
# The crew roles (CREW-ROLES.tomllmd) define the battle formation:
#
# | Role | Tier | A2A output contract |
# |---|---|---|
# | executor (ralph) | sm0l | PASS/FAIL:<5lines> |
# | implementer | ch0nky | diff+test |
# | architect | frontier | structured decision |
# | orchestrator | frontier | next-task handoff |
#
# The service fabric wraps each role with:
# 1. Bouncer input gate (PRD-008 ControlFlow gate)
# 2. Execution
# 3. OTEL record (PRD-009)
# 4. Postel hint if non-canonical input (PRD-010)
# 5. OKR KR update (PRD-001)

## Knowledge Graph Self-Awareness

# `b00t datums graph --format=owl2` (PRD-005 + PRD-006) produces b00t-ontology.ttl
# The ontology IS the self-documentation:
# - Query: "which skills have ControlFlow gates?" → OWL2 SPARQL
# - Query: "which datums have prd type with priority=1?" → `b00t datum filter --types=prd`
# - Query: "what's the current OKR status?" → `b00t datum filter --types=okr`
# - Query: "which commands ran most this session?" → `b00t session otel --scrape`
#
# First-order logic provability (PRD-006 CLIF axioms):
# - Every PRD datum with priority=1 MUST have at least one KR in an active OKR
# - Every agent role MUST have a bouncer gate
# - Every delegation MUST emit an OTEL record
# These are checked by `b00t validate` (future: wired to pre-commit hook).

## Fine-Tunable MCP Interface

# b00t MCP tools are the inter-process protocol:
# - `mcp__b00t-mcp__b00t_agent_delegate` → delegation
# - `mcp__b00t-mcp__b00t_task_*` → task management
# - `mcp__b00t-mcp__b00t_session_status` → OTEL summary
# Fine-tuning: every A2A call generates a (prompt, tool_call, result) training triple
# in `guard-violations.jsonl` sidecar → feeds sm0l fine-tune on the hive's own calls.

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] PRD-002 TomllmDelta::apply() implemented and dogfooded (50% token reduction)
# - [ ] `/next-task:N` handoff produces machine-readable battle plan in TOML
# - [ ] OODA loop runs one complete cycle without operator intervention
# - [ ] Knowledge graph query returns accurate PRD/OKR/pattern counts
# - [ ] A2A call generates fine-tune training triple in guard-violations.jsonl
# - [ ] `b00t validate` checks first-order logic axioms from PRD-006

